{
  "id": "fraternalistic-relative-deprivation",
  "term": "fraternalistic relative deprivation",
  "definition": "Fraternalistic relative deprivation is the feeling that one’s own group is unfairly worse off than another group or is not getting the status or resources it should have. It is based on how people judge their group’s position relative to other groups, and it can occur even when objective conditions do not match that perception.",
